.TH TEE 1 "September 19, 2026" maux
.SH NAME
tee \- pipe fitting
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tee
.RB [ \-ai ]
.I file ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Tee
transcribes the standard input to the standard output and makes copies
in the named files.
At least one, and at most five, file operands are required.
.TP
.B \-a
Append to each named file.
.TP
.B \-i
Ignore interrupt signals.
.PP
A failed destination is reported and skipped; copying to the other
destinations and standard output continues.
For example:
.PP
.B cat input | tee copy
.SH FILES
/usr/man/TEE  this page
.SH "SEE ALSO"
cat(1), cp(1), licenses(1)
.SH DIAGNOSTICS
Exit status is 0 on success, 1 for a destination open/write failure, 2 for usage errors.
.SH BUGS
Without -a, writing begins at offset zero but an existing longer file is not shortened. Use a new or empty destination when an exact copy is required.
